--- a/doc/api.rst
+++ b/doc/api.rst
@@ -447,6 +447,12 @@ The library also supports convenient formatting of ranges and tuples::
   fmt::print("{}", t);
 
 
+Character ranges other than strings are formatted as sequences of quoted
+characters, including when nested in other ranges. For example,
+``std::vector<std::vector<char>>{{'a'}, {'b', '-', 'c'}}`` is formatted as
+``[['a'], ['b', '-', 'c']]``. C++20 split and transform views follow the same
+rules; constructibility as a ``std::string_view`` does not make a range a string.
+
 NOTE: currently, the overload of ``fmt::join`` for iterables exists in the main
 ``format.h`` header, but expect this to change in the future.
 
